 4. 💉 GLP-1 black market 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Maura Losch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Eli Lilly's next-generation weight-loss drug — retatrutide, which hasn't even been submitted for FDA review — is already spawning cheap knockoffs heavily touted online.

 Why it matters: Demand for weight-loss drugs is outpacing drug development and regulation, fueling a black-market frenzy, Axios' Tina Reed reports. Catch up quick: Eli Lilly recently filed six lawsuits accusing med spas, at least one compounding pharmacy and other vendors of illegally selling counterfeit retatrutide as a weight-loss "hack."

 Retatrutide is still in clinical trials for obesity, type 2 diabetes and related conditions. No regulator has approved ​the drug for human use, Lilly told Reuters . Influencers have been touting knockoffs dubbed "r3ta" or "triple G." A quick Google search nets dozens of companies selling the drug for as much as $600.

