 6. 🗳️ Stat du jour: Record number of Black gubernatorial candidates 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Rep. Byron Donalds (R-Fla.) speaks at his victory party in Orlando after winning the Republican gubernatorial nomination last Tuesday. Photo: John Raoux/AP Only three of America's elected governors out of thousands have been Black — all Democrats and all men: current Maryland Gov. Wes Moore, former Virginia Gov. L. Douglas Wilder and former Massachusetts Gov. Deval Patrick.

 November ballots will have eight Black major-party gubernatorial nominees, AP reports. The eight (three Rs and five Ds): Republicans Byron Donalds in Florida, Lisa Demuth in Minnesota and John James in Michigan … plus Democrats Aaron Ford in Nevada, Keisha Lance Bottoms in Georgia, Jermaine Johnson in South Carolina, David Crowley in Wisconsin and Wes Moore, up for reelection in Maryland. 

