 7. 🎙️ Trump forgives former fixer 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Michael Cohen speaks during a news conference announcing his new radio show. Photo: Seth Wenig/AP President Trump signaled that he's welcomed his former fixer, Michael Cohen, back into the fold in a friendly interview that aired in full yesterday.

 The interview was taped for Cohen's new radio show , "When You Know, You Know," on 77 WABC in New York. It's the first time Trump and Cohen have spoken publicly since Cohen was a key witness in the hush money trial that led to Trump's conviction on 34 felony counts of falsifying business records, Axios' Josephine Walker and Avery Lotz report. 👀 Trump and Cohen have repeatedly traded barbs over each other's alleged wrongdoing. Cohen previously called Trump a "conman" and a "predator," while the president said Cohen was a "rat."

 In the interview, they buried the hatchet. Trump blamed New York Attorney General Letitia James and Manhattan District Attorney Alvin Bragg for Cohen's role in the hush money trial: "They threatened you with everything if you didn't go against Trump, and you took it back. I wouldn't even be talking to you right now if you didn't." Share this story . 

 
 
