 8. 🏁 1 for the road: D.C. Prix 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump waves the green flag to start the Freedom 250 Grand Prix race with first lady Melania Trump at his side. Photo: Doug Mills/The New York Times Axios D.C.'s Gabe Hiatt reports from D.C.'s first IndyCar race: 

 Military flyovers buzzed above the National Mall. Race cars roared past the Capitol at 180 mph. President Trump waved the green flag.

 The race marking America's 250th birthday got an American winner. Florida driver Kyle Kirkwood celebrated alongside a bald eagle. Kyle Kirkwood after winning yesterday's Freedom 250 Grand Prix. Photo: Eric Lee/Getty Images The National Mall felt like a giant national picnic. Fans sprawled across the grass and packed shaded tents between games of cornhole and ladder golf. 

 President Trump rides in "The Beast" ahead of the race yesterday. Photo: Daniel Heuer/Reuters Trump took a ceremonial lap around the track in the presidential limousine, known as "The Beast."

 Spectators watch drivers compete during yesterday's Freedom 250 Grand Prix. Photo: Alex Kent/The New York Times Seven flyovers thundered overhead, including a low-flying Air Force One — shaking the ground.

